00:02:47.000 --> 00:03:12.000
Well, this was the greatest fun. The British Museum is created in the middle of the 18th century. Really, at that moment of the Enlightenment, when people begin to have a totally different notion of what humanity means, it's the physical expression of that enlightenment notion that there is one humanity. So what we decided to do was to try to organise the 100 objects.

6
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:42.000
Well, the BBC decided that there would be five programmes a week and there needed to be a theme for each week. And we wanted to go effectively from the beginning, the earliest hand tools made by anything that can roughly be called human right up to today. So that gave us the format. And that in each week we would go round the world. So you would take, let's say, you know, 1,000 BCE and look at a theme, let's say, power.

